TITLE:: REShowConsole
summary:: HadronLake3's show console: Reaper's clock to the effects page, the takes' control tapes chased to it, the Roto mixed in
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REShowChase, Classes/REShowRoto, Classes/REKnobMix, Classes/REVisualsTape, Classes/RCVisuals

DESCRIPTION::
At HadronLake3's live performance (Oct 31 2026) Reaper plays the pieces' audio stems and owns the clock. This console, sclang without a server, receives Reaper's OSC control surface, applies one venue offset, sends the show clock to HomewareVisuals' effects page through the bridge (link::Classes/RCVisuals::), replays each cue's control tape chased to that clock (link::Classes/REShowChase::) and mixes the Roto-Control's knobs into the tapes' values (link::Classes/REShowRoto::, link::Classes/REKnobMix::). The page's side (chase mode: code::/fx/chase::, code::/fx/cue::, code::/fx/time::, code::/fx/transport::) is HomewareVisuals' effects page; HomewareSC's code::scripts/console.sh:: starts one from a show file.

subsection:: The show file
JSON (link::Classes/REJSON::), paths relative to its folder:
code::
{ "offset": 0.0, "port": 57150, "rate": 15,
  "cues": [ { "name": "symbolic", "take": "Scores/<take>.json", "video": "symbolic.mp4",
              "start": 0.0, "end": 123.4, "videoOffset": 0.0 }, ... ],
  "roto": { "device": "Roto-Control", "glide": 1.0,
            "knobs": [ { "cc": 0, "ctl": "symbolic_wave", "op": "add", "range": [-0.5, 0.5] },
                       { "cc": 1, "set": ["colour", "mix"], "range": [0, 1] } ] } }
::
A cue's tape is its take's control tape, named code::ctl:: by the take's render sidecar (code::<take>.render.json::: code::<take>/<take>.ctl.json::, HomewareSC's code::take.sh render --viz::); without one the sidecar's code::tape:: (the code::.viz.json::) is read and kept to its code::/fx/:: entries; a cue may name a code::tape:: itself instead of a take. code::end:: defaults to code::start:: plus the sidecar's code::duration:: (else the cue's own code::duration::, else the tape's length, said); code::videoOffset:: to 0; code::video:: is passed to the page as written (a URL it can load). code::start:: and code::end:: are on the show clock, Reaper's timeline plus the offset (a small venue latency: write Reaper positions). The tapes are read at start (link::Classes/REVisualsTape#*read::, synchronous: control tapes are small).

subsection:: The protocol
Reaper → console, UDP on the console's port (57150; Reaper's OSC control surface with its default patterns): code::/time <seconds>::, code::/play <0|1>::, code::/stop <0|1>::, code::/pause <0|1>::. The transport is also derived from code::/time:: alone: a time that has not advanced for link::#-staleAfter:: (0.3 s) is a pause; one more than link::#-jumpTolerance:: (0.5 s) off the extrapolation is a seek; one that starts advancing in step with real time while stopped is a start.

Console → page (code::RCVisuals.sendArgs::, through the bridge): code::/fx/chase <0|1>:: at start and stop; code::/fx/cues:: (every cue removed) then code::/fx/cue <name> <video> <start> <end> <videoOffset>:: per cue, at start and at a reload; code::/fx/time <t>::, the show clock t = Reaper's time + offset, link::#-rate:: times a second while playing and once at a seek or a stop (the page lands where Reaper is); code::/fx/transport <0|1>::; and the control tape's entries as recorded, at their show time (the heartbeat advances the cue's chase from the previous tick's time; a seek, a start and a cue entered send the state); code::/fx/start::, code::/fx/stop:: and code::/fx/page:: never. A mapped code::/fx/ctl:: (a Roto knob's) carries the mix's value in place of the tape's. Every handler and every tick is guarded (link::Classes/RCGuard::): one bad entry never kills the console.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: show
The show file's path, or an Event / dictionary already read (then code::dir:: in it is the folder its paths are relative to).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: start
The port opened and its handlers installed, the cues' tapes read, the roto started (its MIDI with link::#-startMidi::), the page told (code::/fx/chase 1::, code::/fx/cues::, the code::/fx/cue:: lines), the heartbeat on SystemClock (with link::#-heartbeat::). Nothing plays until Reaper speaks. With link::#-live:: the sends go to the user's bridge, 127.0.0.1:57300.
METHOD:: stop
The heartbeat, the handlers and the roto freed, code::/fx/transport 0:: when playing, code::/fx/chase 0::.
METHOD:: reload
The show file read again (when the console was given one), the cues rebuilt and sent again, the chase landed where the clock is.

METHOD:: timeReceived
Reaper's time, seconds: what the code::/time:: handler calls. A jump off the extrapolation while playing, or a change while stopped, lands the page there; a time advancing in step with real time while stopped starts the transport.
argument:: secs
METHOD:: transportReceived
1 (or true): playing; 0: stopped or paused. What the code::/play::, code::/stop:: and code::/pause:: handlers call.
argument:: flag
METHOD:: tick
One beat of the heartbeat at code::now::: playing, the show clock sent and the cue's chase advanced from the previous tick (a cue entered: its state); a stale time, the transport derived stopped; the roto's gliding mixes sent. Returns the show time sent, nil when stopped.
argument:: now

METHOD:: time
The show clock now (nil before Reaper said anything).
METHOD:: playing
METHOD:: cueAt
The cue at a show time: the last started among those holding it (code::start <= t < end::), nil between cues.
argument:: t
METHOD:: cueNamed
argument:: name
METHOD:: cues
Sorted by start, each an Event: code::name::, code::video::, code::start::, code::end::, code::videoOffset::, code::tape:: (the path read), code::take::, code::chase:: (the link::Classes/REShowChase::).
METHOD:: currentCue
The cue whose chase the heartbeat advances.
METHOD:: roto
The link::Classes/REShowRoto::, nil without a code::"roto":: in the show.
METHOD:: status
One line posted and returned.

METHOD:: port
The UDP port Reaper sends to (57150; the show's code::port::). Set before start.
METHOD:: offset
The venue offset, seconds, live: the show clock is Reaper's time plus it (the show's code::offset::).
METHOD:: rate
Heartbeats a second (15; the show's code::rate::).
METHOD:: live
True: code::RCVisuals.setAddr("127.0.0.1", 57300)::, the user's bridge, whatever the environment says (HomewareSC's code::scripts/console.sh --live::); false (the default): RCVisuals as it stands (a headless run's own bridge or an unbound port).
METHOD:: heartbeat
The heartbeat Routine at start (true); a test ticks by hand.
METHOD:: startMidi
The roto's MIDI at start (true); a test leaves it.
METHOD:: staleAfter
METHOD:: jumpTolerance
METHOD:: sendFunc
code::{ |path, args| }::; code::RCVisuals.sendArgs:: by default. The chases and the roto send through it.
METHOD:: timeFunc
code::{ seconds }::; code::Main.elapsedTime:: by default.
METHOD:: lastTime
Reaper's last time.
METHOD:: started
METHOD:: ticks
METHOD:: show
METHOD:: path
METHOD:: dir

EXAMPLES::

code::
c = REShowConsole("~/Music/Supercollider/HomewareSC/Personal_SC/Biomusic_clone/260927_HadronLake3/Reaper/HadronLake3_Show_w0_261031.json");
c.live = true;        // the user's bridge
c.start;              // Reaper: Preferences > Control/OSC/web > OSC, send to 127.0.0.1:57150 with the default patterns
c.offset = 0.08;      // the venue: the picture 80 ms later
c.status;
c.stop;
::
